# Keys allowed to sign Sbarbase releases, read by lab/release_channel.py through
# `git verify-tag` with gpg.format=ssh (the ssh-keygen ALLOWED SIGNERS format).
#
# One line per key:
#   <principal> namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
# for example:
#   maintainer@example.com namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA...
#
# The maintainer adds the public half of the release signing key here, in a commit of
# its own, before the first signed release. Until a key line exists, every release is
# refused as unsigned: that is the intended safe default, not a fault.
